    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0275" n="205" xml:id="pg205"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From Sprague, consul, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-29">29th</date>, 3.30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Inform our government Kearsarge leaves to-morrow for the Azores in pursuit of
                    Semmes, who has destroyed ten whalers. Have recommended Tuscarora, now at Cadiz,
                    to follow her at once, and the Constellation to come down the Mediterranean.</p>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adams,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">American Minister, London.</hi></p>
            </div>
        </body>
